// @run
// @log 3
// @log a
// CONTRACT (must-RUN): the ALIAS spelling of the mixed union. `K`'s members flatten into
// sibling literal members of the union, so the gate sees two literals and a scalar — two
// distinct softened bases, hence the box — and `print` dispatches on its tag (D712).
//
// THE ALIAS ARM IS THE STRING ARM, and that is a fact about the BOX rather than about the
// spelling. The emit NAME keeps `K` un-softened in some positions (a closure RESULT
// registers the alias atom), so `valueAtomKind("K")` is -1 and no per-atom ladder claims it
// — but `emitUnionCoerce`'s `unionTakesAtomAsStr` arm widens the interned id through
// `emitAtomToStr` and tags the box kind 2 with the member STRING riding the anyref. So the
// print dispatch reads tag 2 and streams `a`, the member text. Before D-LITPRINT this
// spelling built invalid wasm; between D-LITPRINT and D712 it was a clean reject.
type K = "a" | "b"
const v: K | i32 = 3
print(v)

const m: K | i32 = "a"
print(m)
